      "end_timestamp": "04:42",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.family_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "So where does that leave us? It fits best with medication-overuse headache on a background of migraine. Tension-type headache is still possible.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:43",
      "end_timestamp": "04:52",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "clinical_assessment[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with medication-overuse headache on a background of migraine do well once it's treated properly. A headache diary is what I'd like next, for daily headache. For this, amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night, long term. It's for headache prevention.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:57",
      "end_timestamp": "05:18",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]",
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Stop the daily painkillers gradually, the headaches may worsen for a couple of weeks first. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:25",
      "end_timestamp": "05:40",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]",
        "clinical_actions[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. Come back in six weeks. Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me?",
      "start_timestamp": "05:46",
      "end_timestamp": "06:00",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]",
